PROPRIETARY SOFTWARE LICENSE AND DISTRIBUTION AGREEMENT
This Agreement (the "Agreement") is a legal contract between the Licensor and the Distributor. It grants the Distributor a limited, non-exclusive right to distribute the Software to end users, while strictly protecting the Licensor's proprietary rights.

1. GRANT OF DISTRIBUTION LICENSE

The Licensor grants the Distributor a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right to market, distribute, and sublicense the Software to end users ("Licensees") within a specified territory.

2. END USER RESTRICTIONS

The Distributor must ensure that every end user accepts a binding End User License Agreement (EULA) before accessing the Software. This EULA must strictly prohibit end users from:
• Reverse engineering, decompiling, disassembling, or modifying the Software.
• Redistributing, renting, leasing, or transferring the Software to third parties.
• Accessing or exposing the source code of the Software.

3. PROHIBITIONS ON THE DISTRIBUTOR

The Distributor shall not:
• Modify or alter the Software, its source code, branding, or proprietary notices in any way.
• Sublicense or assign its distribution rights to sub-distributors without prior written consent from the Licensor.
• Copy the Software except for authorized distribution or archival purposes.

4. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY & OWNERSHIP

All title, ownership, and intellectual property rights in the Software remain exclusively with the Licensor. This Agreement only grants a license to distribute copies; it does not transfer any ownership or copyright interest.

5. TERMINATION

The Licensor may terminate this distribution agreement immediately if the Distributor breaches any term. Upon termination, the Distributor must cease all distribution, marketing, and sales of the Software and destroy or return all copies in their possession.
